@prefix : <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498/1.0.0#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix xml: <http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@base <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498/1.0.0#> .

<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498/1.0.0> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                           owl:imports <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989/1.0.0> ,
                                                       <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498/1.0.0> ,
                                                       <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682/1.0.0> ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract> "An alignment ontology describing artificial intelligence applications in automated plants together with the plant and the technical process it runs. It imports three subdomain patterns, for the technical process after VDI/VDE 3682, for communication after ISO/IEC 7498-1 and for artificial intelligence after ISO/IEC 22989, and ties them together through three collecting classes: a function, a component and a relation. Placing a process operator and an inference under one function class is what makes them comparable, so that the same assignment states which resource carries out which function, whichever subdomain that function comes from. Twelve own classes and eight own relations. Nothing here is normative: the patterns rest on standards, the alignment rests on design decisions."@en ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/bibliographicCitation> "M. Schieseck, P. Topalis, L. Reinpold, F. Gehlhoff and A. Fay, \"A Formal Model for Artificial Intelligence Applications in Automation Systems,\" 2024 IEEE 29th International Conference on Emerging Technologies and Factory Automation (ETFA), Padova, Italy, IEEE, September 2024. DOI 10.1109/ETFA61755.2024.10710890"@en ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2024-09-01"^^xsd:date ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Alexander Fay" ,
                                                                              "Felix Gehlhoff" ,
                                                                              "Lasse Reinpold" ,
                                                                              "Marvin Schieseck" ,
                                                                              "Philip Topalis" ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> <https://w3id.org/aias> ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-09-02"^^xsd:date ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> "Helmut-Schmidt-Universität / Universität der Bundeswehr Hamburg" ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "R. Haberfellner, O. de Weck, E. Fricke and S. Vössner, Systems Engineering. Springer, 2019. ISBN 978-3-030-13430-3"@en ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/rights> "This research is funded by dtec.bw – Digitalization and Technology Research Center of the Bundeswehr. dtec.bw is funded by the European Union – NextGenerationEU"@en ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/subject> "Artificial Intelligence"@en ,
                                                                              "Automated Plant"@en ,
                                                                              "Industrial Automation"@en ,
                                                                              "Ontology Alignment"@en ,
                                                                              "System Architecture"@en ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "AIAS Alignment Ontology"@en ;
                                           <http://purl.org/ontology/bibo/doi> "10.1109/ETFA61755.2024.10710890" ;
                                           <http://purl.org/ontology/bibo/status> "Draft"@en ;
                                           <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespacePrefix> "aias" ;
                                           <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespaceUri> "https://w3id.org/aias#" ;
                                           rdfs:comment """Nothing here is normative. The three patterns rest on standards, this ontology rests on design decisions of the work.

Three subdomains are joined: the technical process after VDI 3682, the communication after ISO/IEC 7498-1, and the AI after ISO/IEC 22989.

Scope: the three patterns named above and the classes that tie them together. The payload of a transmission is equated with a dataset rather than kept apart from it."""@en ;
                                           owl:versionInfo "1.0.0" ;
                                           <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/fundedBy> <https://dtecbw.de/> ;
                                           <https://schema.org/codeRepository> <https://github.com/schiesem/aias> .

